    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (75.28), who represent our highest-ceiling plays against favorable matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits immensely from a soft spot against Curry, whose 5.68 xERA suggests a prime opportunity for extra-base hits. Despite batting in the seven-hole, **Kyle Tucker** remains a elite play; he benefits from a 19% boost due to the high-xERA profile of Abbott, and his ability to contribute across all categories\u2014particularly in a league where speed is at a premium\u2014makes him an essential anchor. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.84) and **Jackson Merrill** (71.56) round out our top-tier group; **Jackson Merrill** specifically draws a 14% park-factor surge that elevates his raw projection into strong-start territory.\n\nStrategic platoon and matchup edges are keeping **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.91) in the lineup despite a slight dip from his base projection due to a negative platoon split. While the matchup against Montero is respectable, he remains a high-floor play who can capitalize on the favorable SP skill rating. The most difficult decision this morning was evaluating the bench, where **Miguel Vargas** (47.59) was the primary consideration. Ultimately, **Miguel Vargas** fell short of the starting rotation because his efficiency profile against Messick failed to outpace the collective value offered by the rest of the infield and utility spots. **Nasim Nunez** (39.48) also failed to crack the lineup, falling below our strict \"Zebras Floor\" threshold, largely due to a combination of a stingy matchup against Wheeler and a disadvantageous nine-hole batting position.\n\nManaging the roster remains a delicate balance as we monitor the health of our depth, with **Andy Pages** and **Jordan Westburg** continuing to occupy critical IL slots. We have no major weather-related risks on the radar for this evening, but keep a close eye on **Drake Baldwin**, whose score of 56.70 is heavily dependent on his #2 spot in the order; any late-breaking lineup changes shifting him lower would necessitate immediate re-evaluation of his status. With the current configuration, we are prioritizing high-xERA targets to maximize our 5x5 production while preserving our game caps.",
